      {
        "id": 247256,
        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-08-10T23:19:25.440Z",
        "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/c/c611cf827ac9c9d476833eeb8758293693a14746.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/c611cf827ac9c9d476833eeb8758293693a14746\" title=\"Screenshot_20220810-181037\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/c/c611cf827ac9c9d476833eeb8758293693a14746_2_225x500.jpeg\" alt=\"Screenshot_20220810-181037\" data-base62-sha1=\"sgcHhGQRBBaQKhVkPcHdIHqFydw\" width=\"225\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/c/c611cf827ac9c9d476833eeb8758293693a14746_2_225x500.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/c/c611cf827ac9c9d476833eeb8758293693a14746_2_337x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/c/c611cf827ac9c9d476833eeb8758293693a14746_2_450x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/c/c611cf827ac9c9d476833eeb8758293693a14746_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">Screenshot_20220810-181037</span><span class=\"informations\">720×1600 99 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>I am just not good at keeping Fanatic alive.  It was entirely her own fault she died though; having discarded Consecrated Ground in order to keep Prayer of Desperation on hand, and never actually played it, she could not make Forced Deployment happen before the Environment turn, when two Oxygen Leaks would have deployed the army right back where they came from.  Instead, even without Vyktor’s leadership, the army of Qubrins, Piunites and Maerynians were able to take her down, but meanwhile the two-and-a-half men finished Voss off.</p>\n<p>The Grand Warlord just doesn’t tend to survive for long against his nemesis, particularly when he fails to bring any ships or guards.  Meanwhile, Guise managed to securely store all three Prime Warden promos, though he only picked up Fanatic after she went down.  All told, a very satisfying match, set of course to one of my favorites of the Environment themes (third or fifth favorite, something like that).</p>",
