      {
        "id": 247263,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-08-11T12:35:00.962Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Oh, right! Personal jargon!</p>\n<p>With Completionist Guise and Fanatic on the same team, you can use a technique I like to call the Fanatic Blender.</p>\n<p>Step 0) Make sure Fanatic is on her Xtreme variant. You can now begin.</p>\n<p>Step 1) Fanatic uses her base power on whatever target you want to utterly destroy.</p>\n<p>Step 2) Guise switches her to Prime Wardens and also uses her power on said target.</p>\n<p>Step 3) Prime Wardens Fanatic uses her base power, dealing 3 radiant damage to the target, getting a free card play, and giving someone a power use. (It’s better not to give this to Guise and just let him do his thing on his turn.) Bonus points if she has Sacrosanct Martyr out, that’s another 5 damage!</p>\n<p>Step 4) Guise swaps Fanatic back to Xtreme, uses the Prime Wardens power, and repeats the above effects. Minus Sacrosanct.</p>\n<p>Step 5) Repeat until victory.</p>\n<p>But every time I had Fanatic do this, Kill the Spirit never took for some reason. Guise could do the one-two combo just fine. There’s video of my attempt here, around 13:30: <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/videos/1556406292\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Twitch</a></p>",
        "post_number": 9,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-08-11T12:35:16.213Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 19,
        "readers_count": 18,
        "score": 33.8,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 29568,
        "topic_slug": "weekly-one-shot-347-a-bit-of-a-stretch",
        "display_username": "KateWalker",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "link_counts": [
          {
            "url": "https://www.twitch.tv/videos/1556406292",
            "internal": false,
            "reflection": false,
            "title": "Twitch",
            "clicks": 1
          }
        ],
        "read": false,
        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "Oh, right! Personal jargon!\n\nWith Completionist Guise and Fanatic on the same team, you can use a technique I like to call the Fanatic Blender.\n\nStep 0) Make sure Fanatic is on her Xtreme variant. You can now begin.\n\nStep 1) Fanatic uses her base power on whatever target you want to utterly destroy.\n\nStep 2) Guise switches her to Prime Wardens and also uses her power on said target.\n\nStep 3) Prime Wardens Fanatic uses her base power, dealing 3 radiant damage to the target, getting a free card play, and giving someone a power use. (It's better not to give this to Guise and just let him do his thing on his turn.) Bonus points if she has Sacrosanct Martyr out, that's another 5 damage!\n\nStep 4) Guise swaps Fanatic back to Xtreme, uses the Prime Wardens power, and repeats the above effects. Minus Sacrosanct.\n\nStep 5) Repeat until victory.\n\nBut every time I had Fanatic do this, Kill the Spirit never took for some reason. Guise could do the one-two combo just fine. There's video of my attempt here, around 13:30: https://www.twitch.tv/videos/1556406292",
